  Code: scripts/
      Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0)
      Full text: added to LICENSES/ with the first file of code - REUSE
      refuses a licence text that no file uses yet

  Everything else: models/, the README and the figures
      Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
      Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

Every file states its own licence, following the REUSE specification
(https://reuse.software/): an SPDX-License-Identifier header in the file, or
an entry in REUSE.toml for files that cannot carry one.

A part keeps the licence it was published under where it came from: the
USB-C panel plate was CC-BY-4.0 in the 3d-printing toolkit, and stays so.

